  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "At the moment, it is extremely easy to modify and hack the VRChat client to go around and steal other people's avatars. I think the internal files of the game should be compressed into one file, of a proprietary format, to prevent easy modification. It might also be wise to have a checksum for the resources file, so when the game executes, it can determine if it has been modded or not.\n\nI believe this would stop a majority of the hackers within this game, and allow people like me to play without worrying that my avatar is going to be stolen if I'm not careful.",
